# froggerpro_stock_port.te - port stock SELinux types missing from our tree
# generated by ~/nphone/bootrec/gen_stock_port.py - do not hand-edit
#
# Evidence (two independent bugs, same cause):
#   1) haptics: init refused to start /vendor/bin/sfdc_param_calibration
#      (labeled vendor_file, no domain transition) so libics_haptic never
#      initializes sfdc -> "actuator has not inited" -> no vibration.
#   2) fingerprint: our vendor_property_contexts lacks
#      persist.vendor.overlay.fp_{model,algo,vendor,serial} so they fall back
#      to plat generic "persist.vendor.overlay." -> overlay_prop (a platform
#      type) which the vendor HAL cannot set -> avc denied -> no fingerprint.
#   Root cause: our tree never carried the stock context/type definitions, so
#   stock vendor binaries land on generic platform types and get denied.
#
# Source: stock OTA vendor_sepolicy.cil (Nothing 4a Pro, Android 16 / 202404)


